// §5.8.1: "If any of the conditionally-executed statements contains an analog
// operator, the conditional expression shall be a analysis_or_constant_
// expression." `V(c) > 0.0` is neither — a probe moves on every Newton
// iteration — so this module is illegal and E0514 rejects it.
//
// The rule is worth enforcing because the failure is invisible otherwise: an
// analog operator is a state machine the kernel advances once per accepted
// step, so the step on which this branch is off feeds `laplace_nd` the type's
// zero instead of the real input, and its history is wrong from then on. The
// residual keeps looking ordinary.
//
// The two carve-outs §5.8.1 does grant — `analysis()` and a `parameter` — are
// pinned in lower.zig's "§5.8.1 an analog operator under a runtime condition"
// test, which walks six conditions past the same operator.
module ch5_conditional_filter(p, c);
  inout p, c; electrical p, c;
  analog if (V(c) > 0.0)
    I(p) <+ laplace_nd(V(p), '{1.0}, '{1.0, 1.0});
endmodule
